liquid_glass_renderer 1.0.0-dev.1, vendored into morph as its glass renderer.

Since 2026-10-03 this is morph's own renderer (lib/src/glass/renderer),
tuned freely; it was vendored under example/third_party before. It stays
Apache-2.0 (LICENSE, NOTICE); the third_party/ notices cover adapted
shader code.

Upstream:  https://github.com/whynotmake-it/flutter_liquid_glass
Branch:    main
Commit:    3cec75eda468f9c6e481bd90b7533dcb5e997b8e (2026-10-06)
Path:      packages/liquid_glass_renderer
License:   Apache-2.0 (LICENSE), copyright Tim Lehmann for whynotmake.it;
           third_party/ keeps the Flutter (BSD) and Inigo Quilez (MIT)
           notices for adapted shader code.

Copied: LICENSE, lib/, third_party/; hook/build.dart and the shader
bundle manifest moved to the morph package root (hook/build.dart,
morph_glass.shaderbundle.json), the shaders to shaders/ here, the
dependencies and the shader asset list to morph's pubspec.yaml.
Left out: README.md, CHANGELOG.md, pubspec.yaml, doc/, example/, test/,
coverage/, analysis_options.yaml (it includes lintervention, a dev
dependency of the upstream repo). The sources are upstream's except for
the local patches listed below.

