- 2026-10-09 analytic geometry: a layer whose frame has no fused field,
  1 to 8 shapes (RenderLiquidGlassLayer.analyticMaxShapes), no geometry
  of two or more shapes with a blend, and one appearance or appearances
  that differ only by tint evaluates its shapes in the final shader
  instead of rendering the Flutter GPU matte and material map:
  shaders/analytic_geometry.glsl (included by the core under
  ANALYTIC_GEOMETRY) runs the geometry pass's own sceneSample (gpu/sdf.glsl,
  with SCENE_SAMPLE_INDEX carrying the winning shape for the tint; the
  geometry and material passes do not define it and compile as before),
  optics and empty-pixel rejection per fragment, and maps the signed
  distance and displacement through the matte's encode and decode ranges,
  so only the matte's quantization and nearest sampling are gone; the
  tint variants take the nearest shape's tint, as the material map does
  without blends. Four final shaders (liquid_glass_final_render_analytic,
  _analytic_ios27, _analytic_tint, _analytic_tint_ios27) declare only the
  background sampler and take the shapes as uniform arrays from float
  index 65 (uAnalyticOptics, uAnalyticRanges, uShapeData, uRseData,
  uShapeBounds, uShapeTints). They are not in ShaderKeys.liquidGlassRenders:
  their programs load (RenderLiquidGlassLayer.precacheAnalyticShaders) only
  while analytic geometry is enabled, outside the liquid capability, each
  layer creates its four shaders once they have loaded, and a program
  that fails to load (a debugRuntimeRoot copy without them) leaves the
  matte path. Analytic shapes are not moved onto a raster grid (no
  raster-phase shifts, bias or phase watch); a uniformly translated frame
  moves their centers and boxes. Every other frame takes the matte path,
  unchanged, in the same frame. Off by default:
  `--dart-define=MORPH_ANALYTIC_GEOMETRY=true` (ShaderKeys
  .analyticGeometry) or RenderLiquidGlassLayer.debugAnalyticGeometry, whose
  setter asks every attached layer for a new geometry frame; the warm-up
  draws the analytic shaders only then. Unit tests:
  test/analytic_geometry_test.dart (uniform layout against the GLSL,
  eligibility); host A/B against the matte and the gallery's Navigation
  layers: example/test/analytic_geometry_host_test.dart,
  example/test/analytic_gallery_host_test.dart.
