  BackdropFilterLayer (and the frost seed); no capture is registered.
  New uniform uSolidBackdrop (vec4, float indices 65-68, after
  uBackdropShrinkAxis): with alpha 1 every backdrop read (refraction,
  dispersion, softening, the undisplaced texel fetch) returns its color,
  a branch uniform across the draw. The analytic uniforms move by 4
  (uAnalyticOptics 69, uAnalyticFlatFace 309, uFusedBoxes 310,
  uShapeTints 342 fused / 310 separate). Over a solid backdrop the
  fragment coordinates are the picture's canvas coordinates, so
  syncCoordinateMapping writes basis dpr and offset -paintOffset x dpr
  (the matte is layer-local device pixels), constant under compositor
  motion; uSize gets the drawn rect's device size (only reads divide by
  it). The common uniforms write uSolidBackdrop as zero (a new
  FragmentShader's uniform buffer is NOT zeroed - SkData::MakeUninitialized
  - and a freed solid shader's color showed up in the next layer's filter
  on the host), and a layer leaving solid mode zeroes it again in the
  shader it wrote. The frozen baseline core
  (example/shader_audit/baseline) declares the uniform, unread, to keep
  the layout the layer writes. The fake layer ignores it. Host A/B
  against the filter over the same color:
  example/test/solid_backdrop_host_test.dart. The pipeline warm-up also
  paints every final variant it warms (matte and analytic) once as that
  drawRect with an opaque uSolidBackdrop, from a FragmentShader instance
  of its own that it zeroes afterwards (the solid paint is a pipeline of
  its own on Impeller: source over into the current pass, not a filter);
  RenderLiquidGlassLayer.solidBackdropUniform names float index 65.
